    "history": {
      "answer": "Croydon King (GSQ site 479076, 8.5 km se of croydon) is recorded by the Geological Survey of Queensland as abandoned mine, gold size band small, 0.5 - 5 t. Reported production: 539.86 kg gold, about 17,357 oz troy (converted here; the survey records 539.86 kg) (to 1933, Croydon King, per GSQ MINOCC 2017 (Total_Ores_Prod, SITE_NO 479076)); 7,973 tonnes ore (to 1933, Croydon King, per GSQ MINOCC 2017 (Total_Ores_Prod, SITE_NO 479076)). GSQ MINOCC 2017 also lists 1 dated Production row (gold: 539.86 kg to 1933); see production. Ownership and tenure: Jko Mining Pty Limited per GSQ MINOCC 2017 (Tenure, SITE_NO 479076). GSQ MINOCC 2017 lists 6 company reports for this site: CR 2946, CR 4868, CR 9568, CR 20314, CR 20315, CR 20971. Not found: closure: no closure year or reason in the sources indexed for this site.",
