    "survey": {
      "answer": "Croydon King (Geological Survey of Queensland site 479076) is recorded as an abandoned mine on the Croydon 1:100,000 sheet (8.5 km se of croydon.), at -18.2550, 142.3030, located to within 50 m. The survey classes its gold as small, 0.5-5 t, and also records silver (very small). Within 5 km it records 32 other historical workings, 32 of them with gold. The record gives a size band, not production figures, and holds no owners or closure dates.",
